  "title": "Balance is read on one territory",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Under the doubling law with open births from the n x n tube, for every schedule a contact binds a ring exactly when its translate by an original lattice vector binds the ring's translate, so a stage's balance is decided by the contacts of one fundamental domain's rings and by those rings' born cells alone (Lemma 1); and every ring born at a doubling is bound at every later lag of its stage (Lemma 2, by the transfer lemma), so an unbalanced stage fails at a ring that lived through a run.",
